      "problem": "Find the coefficient of $x^{4}$ in the expansion of ${\\left( {3 + x} \\right)^{7}} .$",
      "worked_solution": "The binomial theorem states that for any positive integer $n,$ we have\n\n \n\n$$\n{(a + b)^n} = {n \\choose 0}{a^n}{b^0} + {n \\choose 1}{a^{n - 1}}{b^1} + {n \\choose 2}{a^{n - 2}}{b^2} +  \\cdots  + {n \\choose n}{a^0}{b^n}.\n$$\n\nIn the case of ${\\left( {3 +x} \\right)^{7}},$ we have $a=3,$ $b=x,$ and $n=7.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3+x)^{7}=(\\frac{7}{0}){3}^{7}{x}^{0}+(\\frac{7}{1}){3}^{7-1}{x}^{1}+(\\frac{7}{2}){3}^{7-2}{x}^{2}+\u22ef+(\\frac{7}{7}){3}^{7-7}{x}^{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom here, we see that the $x^4$ term must be\n\n$$\n{7 \\choose 4}{3^{7 - 4}}{x^4}.\n$$\n\nEvaluating the coefficient, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\frac{7}{4}){3}^{7-4} & =35\\cdot {3}^{3} \\\\  & =35\\cdot 27 \\\\  & =945.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coefficient of $x^{4}$ is $945.$",
